From ecacf79938b74817e48ddf9915902b32de8ca1fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien MOYAUX <49562406+adrienm7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:07:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(layouts): add the shared layout manager window on three
 drivers

The registry catalogue needs one place where a user sees each layout's
name, author, licence and version with its status, and installs, updates,
uninstalls or selects it. _shared/ui/layout_manager is that page for every
driver: it decides the rows once from one state shape, so the three hosts
only report facts (the catalogue, the installed record, the operation in
flight, the active layout).

Each host accepts an allowlist of actions and checks every layout id
against the catalogue or the installed record before it acts, and opens
only the https homepage the catalogue gives, never a URL the page sends.
macOS and Linux share manager_bridge.lua; Windows mirrors it in its
WebView2 host. A JS DOM test pins the rows, the buttons, the error and
result lines, the busy state and the identical action list of the page
and the three hosts, and every string exists in the 21 locales.
